{
  "about": "Who may call each lososd route. Read by lososd (src/sections.rs) and by modules/identity.nix. Keys are METHOD and the route as http.rs registers it. 'public' needs no sign-in, 'internal' is asked by nginx alone and never served to a client, 'signed-in' needs any person, 'admin' needs losos-admins or the spare key, and a named section needs losos-<name>, losos-admins or (for GET) losos-viewers. A route missing here is admin. 'private' lists the sections losos-viewers do not read. A person in losos-guests may call a 'signed-in' route that changes something only when 'guests' lists it, and a person a moderator muted may not call a route 'speech' lists. 'edge' lists the sections a company edge may use on a box whose owner let it manage the box, besides reading the 'signed-in' routes.",
